  "id": "antipredator-behavior",
  "term": "antipredator behavior",
  "definition": "Antipredator behavior is the set of responses an animal shows to predator-related threats or cues. These responses vary with factors such as age, sex, reproductive state, experience or learning, habitat, temperature, social setting, and especially the kind of predator and the level of predation pressure.",
